# ComposeIO Composer Internal Bus [SPEC:CXC-INTERNAL-BUS]

> Complete namespace registry for the Composer's internal tool bus — the `composer/` namespace tree that wires editor modules together using standard ComposeIO bus semantics.

---

## 1. Bus Configuration [CXC-IBUS-CONFIG]

```yaml
bus_id: composer-internal
scope: local
transport: in-process
heartbeat: false           # No heartbeat needed for in-process bus
discovery: false           # Modules register explicitly at startup
time_sync: false           # Single process; shared clock
```

- rationale: The internal bus is a lightweight in-process message router. Infrastructure services (heartbeat, discovery, time_sync) add overhead without value when all modules share a process and are registered at startup.

---

## 2. Namespace Registry [CXC-IBUS-NAMESPACES]

All internal namespaces use the `composer/` prefix. Organized by functional domain.

### 2.1 Selection Domain

| Namespace | State Engine | Publisher(s) | Subscriber(s) | Description |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `composer/selection/type` | `enum: [none, widget, module, binding, namespace]` | Canvas | Property Editor, Binding Editor, Namespace Inspector | What category of object is selected |
| `composer/selection/widget_id` | string (empty = none) | Canvas | Property Editor, Binding Editor, Preview | ID of selected widget |
| `composer/selection/module_id` | string (empty = none) | Canvas | Property Editor, Binding Editor | ID of selected module |
| `composer/selection/multi` | json list | Canvas | Property Editor, Canvas | Multi-selected widget IDs |
| `composer/selection/binding_id` | string (empty = none) | Canvas, Binding Editor | Property Editor, Canvas | ID of selected binding |

- on-change-only: Selection state follows standard ComposeIO semantics — subscribers are notified only when the value actually changes.
- cascade: Selecting a widget implicitly publishes `module_id` (the widget's parent module) and `type` = `widget`. Modules subscribe to whichever granularity they need.

### 2.2 Palette Domain

| Namespace | State Engine | Publisher(s) | Subscriber(s) | Description |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `composer/palette/selected` | string (widget type name) | Palette | Canvas, Toolbar | Widget type the user wants to place |
| `composer/palette/drag_start` | event | Palette | Canvas | User began dragging a widget from the palette |
| `composer/palette/drag_end` | event | Palette | Canvas | User released drag (with position data) |
| `composer/palette/catalog_changed` | event | Palette | (any) | Widget registry was updated (plugin added/removed) |

### 2.3 Canvas Domain

| Namespace | State Engine | Publisher(s) | Subscriber(s) | Description |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `composer/canvas/widget_added` | event | Canvas | Preview, Namespace Inspector, History | A widget was placed on the canvas |
| `composer/canvas/widget_removed` | event | Canvas | Preview, Namespace Inspector, History | A widget was removed from the canvas |
| `composer/canvas/widget_moved` | event | Canvas | Preview, History | A widget's position changed |
| `composer/canvas/widget_resized` | event | Canvas | Preview, History | A widget's size changed |
| `composer/canvas/module_added` | event | Canvas | Preview, Namespace Inspector, History | A module frame was added |
| `composer/canvas/module_removed` | event | Canvas | Preview, Namespace Inspector, History | A module frame was removed |
| `composer/canvas/layout_changed` | event | Canvas | Preview | Grid weights, column config, or module arrangement changed |
| `composer/canvas/viewport` | continuous (json: {x, y, zoom}) | Canvas | (any) | Current canvas viewport for coordinate transforms |

### 2.4 Configuration Domain

| Namespace | State Engine | Publisher(s) | Subscriber(s) | Description |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `composer/config/widget_changed` | event | Property Editor | Canvas, Preview, History | A widget property was modified |
| `composer/config/module_changed` | event | Property Editor | Canvas, Preview, History | A module-level property was modified |
| `composer/config/namespace_changed` | event | Property Editor, Namespace Inspector | Preview, Binding Editor, History | A namespace definition was modified |

Event data structure for `widget_changed`:
```json
{
  "widget_id": "btn_ftl_arm",
  "property": "led_behavior",
  "old_value": "follow_state",
  "new_value": "blink_500ms",
  "source": "property_editor"
}
```

### 2.5 Binding Domain

| Namespace | State Engine | Publisher(s) | Subscriber(s) | Description |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `composer/binding/created` | event | Binding Editor, Canvas | Preview, Namespace Inspector, Canvas, History | A new binding was defined |
| `composer/binding/modified` | event | Binding Editor | Preview, Namespace Inspector, Canvas, History | An existing binding was changed |
| `composer/binding/removed` | event | Binding Editor, Canvas | Preview, Namespace Inspector, Canvas, History | A binding was deleted |

Event data for `created`:
```json
{
  "binding_id": "bind_001",
  "type": "simple",
  "config": {
    "input_namespace": "sublight_engines",
    "output_namespace": "gauge_power",
    "transform": [{"map": {"off": 0, "half": 50, "full": 100}}]
  }
}
```

### 2.6 Command / History Domain

| Namespace | State Engine | Publisher(s) | Subscriber(s) | Description |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `composer/command/execute` | event | Any module performing a user action | History | Undoable command with forward and reverse params |
| `composer/command/undo` | event | Toolbar, keyboard shortcut handler | History | Request undo of last command |
| `composer/command/redo` | event | Toolbar, keyboard shortcut handler | History | Request redo of last undone command |
| `composer/history/stack_changed` | event | History | Toolbar | Undo/redo availability changed (enables/disables buttons) |

Command event data:
```json
{
  "command_id": "cmd_042",
  "type": "property_change",
  "do": {"widget_id": "btn_1", "property": "label", "value": "FTL Arm"},
  "undo": {"widget_id": "btn_1", "property": "label", "value": "Button 1"},
  "description": "Change label to 'FTL Arm'"
}
```

### 2.7 Tool Mode Domain

| Namespace | State Engine | Publisher(s) | Subscriber(s) | Description |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `composer/tool/mode` | `enum: [select, place, connect, pan]` | Toolbar, keyboard shortcuts | Canvas, Palette, Cursor manager | Current interaction mode |
| `composer/tool/snap_enabled` | `binary` | Toolbar | Canvas | Grid snapping on/off |
| `composer/tool/grid_size` | `continuous_0_255` | Toolbar | Canvas | Grid cell size in pixels |
| `composer/tool/show_bindings` | `binary` | Toolbar | Canvas | Show/hide binding arrows on canvas |

### 2.8 Connection Domain

| Namespace | State Engine | Publisher(s) | Subscriber(s) | Description |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `composer/connection/status` | `enum: [offline, connecting, connected, error]` | Connection | Toolbar, Preview, Bus Monitor | Design bus connection state |
| `composer/connection/transport_added` | event | Connection | Preview, Bus Monitor | A transport was added to the design bus |
| `composer/connection/transport_removed` | event | Connection | Preview, Bus Monitor | A transport was removed |
| `composer/connection/discovery` | event | Connection | Namespace Inspector | Hardware module discovered on design bus |

### 2.9 File Domain

| Namespace | State Engine | Publisher(s) | Subscriber(s) | Description |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `composer/file/dirty` | `binary` | History (on any command) | Toolbar (title bar indicator) | Unsaved changes exist |
| `composer/file/loaded` | event | Toolbar (file open) | All modules | A design file was loaded — full state reset |
| `composer/file/saved` | event | Toolbar (file save) | History (clears dirty flag) | Design was saved to disk |
| `composer/file/path` | string | Toolbar | (any) | Current file path (empty for untitled) |

---

## 3. Message Conventions [CXC-IBUS-CONVENTIONS]

### [CXC-IBUS-CONV-1] Event Data Structure

All events carry a `data` dict with at minimum:
```json
{
  "source": "<module_name>",
  "timestamp": 1711627890.5
}
```

Additional keys are event-specific (documented per namespace above).

### [CXC-IBUS-CONV-2] ID Generation

- widget IDs: `<widget_type_short>_<sequence>` — e.g., `btn_001`, `gauge_002`, `relay_003`
- module IDs: `<module_type>_<sequence>` — e.g., `button_panel_001`, `gauge_panel_001`
- binding IDs: `bind_<sequence>` — e.g., `bind_001`
- command IDs: `cmd_<sequence>` — monotonically increasing per session

### [CXC-IBUS-CONV-3] Null/Empty Convention

- String namespaces use empty string `""` for "no value" (not `null`, not `"none"`).
- List namespaces use empty list `[]` for "no selection".
- This follows ComposeIO convention: state engines always have a value.

### [CXC-IBUS-CONV-4] Batch Operations

When a single user action produces multiple bus messages (e.g., deleting a module removes it and all its widgets), messages carry a shared `batch_id`:
```json
{
  "batch_id": "batch_007",
  "batch_index": 0,
  "batch_total": 4,
  "source": "canvas"
}
```

- undo-behavior: The History module treats an entire batch as a single undoable operation.

---

## 4. Namespace Ownership Rules [CXC-IBUS-OWNERSHIP]

| Rule | Description |
|---|---|
| Single publisher per state namespace | Only one module may publish state to a given namespace. Enforced at registration. |
| Multiple publishers for event namespaces | Events are one-shot; multiple sources are valid (e.g., both Canvas and Binding Editor can publish `composer/binding/removed`). |
| Subscriber count is unbounded | Any module may subscribe to any namespace. |
| `composer/` prefix is reserved | No user-design namespace may use this prefix. Enforced by validation. |
| Namespace documentation is normative | If a namespace is not listed in this document, it does not exist on the internal bus. Adding a namespace requires updating this spec. |

---

## 5. State Engine Definitions [CXC-IBUS-ENGINES]

Custom state engines used by internal namespaces:

### [CXC-IBUS-ENGINE-REJECT-UNIFORM] Out-of-domain rejection is uniform at every ingest BOUNDARY

- error-code: `0x70 ENGINE_VALUE_REJECTED` (`DEC-ERROR-CODE-SEED-SET-V1-2026-08-25`) — `warning` at a boundary that drops it; `critical` on any path that lets it abort the process. This node is what makes the `critical` face impossible rather than merely reported.
- requirement: a state engine RAISES on an out-of-domain value — that is the whole reason a namespace declares an engine (`state_engine.py` `is_valid` / the `current` setter). That raise is load-bearing and MUST be preserved for a PROGRAMMATIC caller of the internal `bus.publish_state` API: a raise there is catchable at the call site and is a real bug signal (pinned by `test_bus_autocreate_engine.py::test_declared_binary_namespace_still_enforces`).
- requirement: BUT a value-ingest **BOUNDARY** — a site where a value crosses into the bus from a context whose exceptions are UNCATCHABLE or process-fatal — MUST convert that rejection into a logged DROP and never let it propagate. The two boundaries are symmetric and MUST behave identically:
  - the EXTERNAL transport boundary (`ComposeIOBus._dispatch_incoming`): a peer's out-of-domain value is a peer contract violation → log-and-drop, keep dispatching (a malformed value must not deafen the bus to the rest of that peer's traffic, nor abort).
  - the RENDER UI boundary (`RenderApp.publish`, through which EVERY widget / gesture / interaction callback funnels via `EngineContext.publish`): an out-of-domain value RAISES inside the native (SDL/Tk) event dispatch, which on macOS becomes an NSException that SIGABRTs the whole surface. A publisher — a finger drag, a `gestures:` producer, an Intelligence `publish()` (control-is-a-peer) — must never be able to kill the surface rendering it → log-and-drop.
- rationale: this contract lived ONLY in code, and only on the external boundary — the render boundary was an unguarded FORK of the same invariant. The concrete crash: a `gestures:` entry that names a namespace but omits `value` publishes the empty string `""` (`states.GesturePublish` default); `""` is the [CXC-IBUS-CONV-3] "no value" string for a STRING namespace but is OUT-OF-DOMAIN for a `binary` engine (`['off','on']`), so one tap on a binary-bound widget aborted the process. A behavior enforced on one boundary and dropped on the other is exactly how a "fixed" crash recurs; naming the invariant here is what stops the CLASS.
- boundary-vs-api: `unknown` ([SPEC:CXC-FRESHNESS]) is a separate, prior gate — it BYPASSES the engine entirely (a category, not a domain member) and is handled before this rule applies. This node governs a genuine domain member miss, not the "I do not know" sentinel.
- test (machine): a UI-boundary publish of an out-of-domain value (incl. `""`) to a declared `binary` namespace DROPS (namespace keeps its last good value) and does NOT raise, across the direct `RenderApp.publish` route AND the `_fire_gesture_publishes` route; the internal `bus.publish_state` API STILL raises for the same value (`python/tests/render/test_ui_publish_boundary_never_aborts.py`).

### [CXC-ENGINE-TOOL-MODE] Tool Mode Engine

```yaml
type: enum
values: [select, place, connect, pan]
default: select
```

- `select`: Click to select widgets, drag to move, handles to resize.
- `place`: Click on canvas to place the widget type from `composer/palette/selected`.
- `connect`: Click source widget, drag to target widget to create binding.
- `pan`: Click and drag to scroll the canvas viewport.

### [CXC-ENGINE-CONNECTION] Connection Status Engine

```yaml
type: enum
values: [offline, connecting, connected, error]
default: offline
```

- `offline`: Design bus has in-process transport only. No external connection.
- `connecting`: Transport connection in progress (MQTT handshake, UART open, etc.).
- `connected`: At least one external transport is active. Hardware messages flowing.
- `error`: Connection attempt failed or was lost. Details in event data.

### [CXC-ENGINE-SELECTION] Selection Type Engine

```yaml
type: enum
values: [none, widget, module, binding, namespace]
default: none
```

- `none`: Nothing selected. Property editor shows design-level properties.
- `widget`: A widget slot is selected. Property editor shows widget config.
- `module`: A module frame is selected. Property editor shows module config.
- `binding`: A binding arrow/card is selected. Property editor shows binding config.
- `namespace`: A namespace entry is selected (in Namespace Inspector). Property editor shows namespace config.

---

## 6. Testing Protocol [CXC-IBUS-TESTING]

### [CXC-IBUS-TEST-1] Namespace Contract Tests

For every namespace in the registry:
1. Verify the publisher module publishes correctly-typed values.
2. Verify subscriber modules handle the full range of state engine values.
3. Verify on-change semantics: duplicate publishes do not trigger subscriber callbacks.

### [CXC-IBUS-TEST-2] Module Isolation Tests

For each module:
1. Instantiate with a mock `ComposeIOBus`.
2. Inject messages on subscribed namespaces.
3. Verify published messages on expected namespaces.
4. Verify no messages published on unexpected namespaces.
5. Verify no direct references to other module instances.

### [CXC-IBUS-TEST-3] Cross-Bus Isolation Tests

1. Publish a message on the internal bus.
2. Verify it does NOT appear on the design bus.
3. Publish a message on the design bus.
4. Verify it does NOT appear on the internal bus.
5. Exception: The Preview module and Bus Monitor subscribe to the design bus directly — verify they receive design bus messages correctly.

